{
  "id": 291348892,
  "iid": 15002,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Retap IO Graph if the Y field changes",
  "description": "If filter assigned to the tap changes, which means the full_filter\nincluding the Y field, then we have to retap.\n\nThis fixes an issue where changing the Y field on an existing\ngraph did not retap and draw a graph with the new information\n(the graph would have to be disabled and reenabled.)\n\nIt also fixes an issue where the changing the Y axis type from\na type that doesn't use the field to one that does wouldn't\nretap and wouldn't display anything (the io_graph_item_t not\nbeing filled in), and changing the other direction would display\ninformation filtered incorrectly in some cases.\n    \nThere's still an issue with switching to and from LOAD graphs,\nbecause they fill in the io_graph_item_t differently from the\nother advanced types.\n\nNote that if someone doesn't want to immediately retap, the\n\"Automatic update\" checkbox can be disabled.",
